This project is built against /docs/Fitness_Tracker_Master_Prompt.md,
/docs/Fitness_Tracker_UIUX_Design_Spec.md, and /docs/UI_Consolidation_Brief_v2.md.
Treat these as the source of truth for features, edge cases, and visual design.
Follow /docs/Revised_Roadmap.md's stage order for what to build next — this
supersedes the original Cursor_Build_Plan.md, which is archived for history
only and should not be used for sequencing. When something is ambiguous or
these docs conflict with a request, ask rather than inventing a default.

Keep README.md accurate. If a commit would change anything the README states
as current fact — test counts, roadmap stage, whether a feature is wired in
the UI, stack versions, or a deployed URL — update README.md in that same
commit. Re-run `npm test` before changing the test-count badge; do not leave
the README overstating the app.
